  "integration.guide_title": "Integration Guide for Developers",
  "integration.guide_desc": "Share this page with your application developer. With one API key, their app can pull attendance data from Netra into their own dashboard. Just call the endpoints below — no complex setup needed.",
  "integration.guide_step1_title": "1. What you need",
  "integration.guide_step1_li1": "An API Key (create one above, click \"Create API Key\"). Keep it safe — treat it like a password.",
  "integration.guide_step1_li2": "The ability to make HTTP requests from your app's backend (any language: PHP, Node, Python, Go, etc.).",
  "integration.guide_step1_li3": "Do NOT put the key in frontend/browser code — only in your application server.",
  "integration.guide_step2_title": "2. Base URL & Authentication",
  "integration.guide_step2_desc": "All endpoints use this base URL. Send the key via the X-API-Key header (or Authorization: Bearer <key>).",
  "integration.guide_step3_title": "3. Endpoint: attendance records",
  "integration.guide_step3_desc": "GET /integration/attendance — attendance list (paginated). Optional filters: from, to (YYYY-MM-DD), user_id, page, limit.",
  "integration.guide_step4_title": "4. Endpoint: daily status (roster)",
  "integration.guide_step4_desc": "GET /integration/attendance/daily-status?date=YYYY-MM-DD — who is present/late/absent on a given day.",
  "integration.guide_step5_title": "5. Sample response",
  "integration.guide_step5_desc": "Always formatted as { \"data\": ..., \"error\": null }. Data is inside data.items.",
  "integration.guide_notes_title": "Notes",
  "integration.guide_notes_li1": "Most endpoints are read-only (safe). The only write is POST /integration/users (scope users:write) — it creates/updates people by external_id and never deletes.",
  "integration.guide_notes_li2": "The key is automatically bound to your organization; other tenants' data will never be included.",
  "integration.guide_notes_li3": "If the key leaks, click Reset to create a new key (old key immediately dies), or Revoke.",
  "integration.guide_notes_li4": "Response 401 = key wrong/revoked/expired. Response 403 = key lacks required scope.",
